module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.observer_inside_its_own_observed_population

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data observer_inside_its_own_observed_population: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "observer_inside_its_own_observed_population" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an observer is a member of the population it observes** (INVALID STATE: a predicate is applied to decide whether some work is live, and the predicate's extension INCLUDES THE PROCESS APPLYING IT, so the observation is satisfied by the act of observing. HARM: the probe answers yes forever, at full confidence, having measured only itself -- and because a long-running job and a self-satisfying probe both present as a steady affirmative for an unbounded time, THE FALSE STATE IS INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM THE HEALTHY ONE by inspection of the answer alone. ",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-05, reported by quick-heron-85 and mechanism confirmed from the matcher's own semantics: a liveness guard shaped `pgrep -f <script>` was used to decide whether compiles were still running. `-f` matches against the FULL COMMAND LINE, and the watcher's command line contains the script name it is searching for, so the guard matches ITSELF BY CONSTRUCTION. Two such guards match each other and hold each other alive indefinitely. GROUND TRUTH WAS ZERO COMPILES RUNNING for roughly forty minutes, while the lane reported MID-RUN twice on the strength of `3 processes alive` -- three watchers watching watchers. Those reports were not stale, they were FALSE, and they were made in good faith from a probe answering exactly what it was asked. ",

    "**THE THREE PROPERTIES THAT MAKE IT EXPENSIVE, and the third is the one that defeats review**: it is SILENT (nothing errors, the probe is working as written); it is INDEFINITE (there is no timeout on a condition that is structurally always true); and it is INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM A LONG RUN (the healthy observation and the degenerate one have the same shape, the same confidence, and the same duration profile). A reader auditing the report sees a plausible number and a running job. There is nothing in the answer to interrogate. ",

    "**THE REMEDY IS ABOUT WHAT THE PREDICATE NAMES, NOT ABOUT EXCLUDING SELF.** The obvious fix -- filter out your own PID -- is the artifact-grained one: it repairs this invocation and leaves the shape, so the next guard written against a wrapper, a shell, a make target or a CI step name reintroduces it, and two SEPARATE watchers still match each other even with self excluded. THE DURABLE FORM IS THAT A LIVENESS CHECK MUST NAME THE EXECUTABLE THAT DOES THE WORK, NEVER A SCRIPT, WRAPPER, OR INVOCATION STRING, because every layer above the executable is TEXT, and text is a thing other processes can be carrying for reasons of their own. `pgrep -x rustc` asks about a program; `pgrep -f build.sh` asks about a string that appears in the command line of anything that mentions it, including the asker. ",

    "**BOUNDARIES, because two rostered rows sit close and neither covers this.** `liveness_probe_read_as_currency` is a CURRENCY error: the probe answers RUNNING correctly and a reader consumes it as running the CURRENT DEFINITION, so the probe's own answer is true. Here the probe's answer is FALSE, and it is false because of who is in its extension. `comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares` is about a key reduced to a PROPER COMPONENT of a composite identity; a command-line substring is not a component of process identity at all but an unrelated surface that merely correlates with it. The distinguishing question for this row is neither currency nor projection: DOES THE ACT OF ASKING SATISFY THE THING ASKED? ",

    "**GENERAL FORM, since the shape is not specific to processes.** Any observation whose subject is identified by a surface the OBSERVER ALSO OCCUPIES is at risk: a log scan whose pattern its own log line matches, a lock probe whose held-lock query is itself a holder, a queue-depth check that enqueues, a mutation census counting its own commit, a scan for a marker string performed by a tool whose source contains the marker string. The tell is available before any measurement: state the predicate, then ask whether the thing evaluating it satisfies it. ",

    "**RUNG AND REMEDY STATE, stated plainly because `a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism` requires it: NOTHING IS HARDER TO DO AFTER THIS ROW LANDS.** No check refuses a self-matching predicate, no lens reads shell text for this shape, and the executable-not-string rule is a discipline carried in prose, which is the carrier this roster has twice today recorded as unable to refuse. RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- the false state produced no diagnostic and was caught by a human comparing a report against ground truth. CEILING: mechanically preventable at best for shell text, because deciding whether an arbitrary matcher's extension contains its own evaluator is not decidable in general; but the SPECIFIC and common form is decidable and is where the trigger belongs. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: a modelled process-liveness operation whose subject is an EXECUTABLE IDENTITY rather than a command-line string, sufficient that a liveness question cannot be ASKED in terms of a matchable text surface -- at which point the invalid state has no constructor rather than being caught by a reviewer who happens to know about `-f`. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
